      "content": "The \"Goblin Test\" is just a silly name I gave to a very important safety rule, but I can't help it, because goblins are everywhere and they love to trip people up before they even start lifting.\n\nTo pick your starting weights without the weird goblin stuff, you need to find your **1 Rep Max (1RM)** or at least a safe percentage of it.\n\nHere is the simple math:\n1.  **Squat:** Try to lift a weight that feels heavy but you can do 3 or 4 times. That's usually around 60-70% of your max.\n2.  **Bench Press:** Lift a weight where you can do 3 reps with good form. Aim for 60-70% of your max.\n3.  **Deadlift:** This is the heaviest one. Lift a weight where you can do 3 reps, but stop if your back feels weird. Aim for 60-70% of your max.\n\n**Why this works:**\nIf you start too light, you'll be bored and won't grow strong like a goblin who finds a hidden treasure. If you start too heavy,",
